Subject: [PATCH] Fail a ByteStream upload whose source is empty but its digest is not

Base: facebook/buck2 9a1876786f32806f6b65fc51f4c1c3077efc38a5 plus the
preceding Sekka patches.

upload_bytestream returned success without sending anything whenever its
source read as empty, a shortcut carried over from upstream's segment
adapter. Only blobs at least the batch limit in size take this path, so
an empty read there means the file was truncated after it was hashed.
The cache uploader then believed the blob was uploaded and wrote an
action-cache entry naming a blob the CAS never received. The function
now takes the digest's size: an empty digest still sends nothing, and an
empty source for a non-empty digest fails the upload. A shorter
non-empty source was already rejected by the server's hash check.

diff --git a/remote_execution/oss/re_grpc/src/client.rs b/remote_execution/oss/re_grpc/src/client.rs
